.TH DANBY-AEROBRAKING 1
.SH NAME
danby-aerobraking \- orbital energy loss during atmospheric passes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/aerobraking
.SH MODEL
Central gravity produces the orbit while exponential atmosphere applies drag
near planetary radius. Repeated periapsis passages lower speed and apoapsis.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Danby-aerobraking
is one file, nothing else: no plugin, no library, no harness. The
problem (central gravity plus atmospheric drag) is written as
.IR eqn (7)
expressions; the diagnostic plot is written in
.IR plot (2)'s
own graph command language; the interface (parameter sliders,
pause/reset) is real Tk, built directly from the same
.B param
lines the physics uses. All of it, problem and interface alike, lives
in one script string this command runs at load time \(em there is no
separate module interface, no separate parsing library, and no
separate harness loaded by path.
.PP
The script is not parsed into a structure and then acted on; it is
.I executed
one line at a time, like a shell script.
.B Cmd
tokenizes each line and passes the words to whichever parser owns
that vocabulary, stopping at the first that claims it \(em it does
.I not
recognize or act on any equation itself. Most of the vocabulary
(.BR param /.BR maxtime /.BR state /.BR derivative /.BR eq /.BR observable )
belongs to
.IR hoc (2)'s
own
.B modelcmd()
(see
.IR hoc (2)
for that language in full); this file's own small remainder is:
.TP
.BI "title " TEXT
Rest of the line, verbatim.
.TP
.BI "bodylabels " "WORD ..."
.TP
.BI "mass " "NUM ..."
One value per
.B bodylabels
word, same order.
.TP
.BI "graph " TEXT
Repeatable, rest of the line verbatim, passed straight to
.IR plot (2)'s
own
.BR Plotter.cmd() :
.BR table / colour
run once, at setup;
.BR axis / line
are reissued every redraw, since
.IR plot (2)'s
own
.B clear
command wipes view/layer state.
.B table
must NOT be reissued \(em
.IR plot (2)'s
own
.B bind()
unconditionally replaces a table with a fresh, empty one, so
reissuing it every redraw would silently erase every appended data
point right after it was recorded. Deciding WHEN each graph command
should run is this app's own business (worked out once a
.IR plot (2)
instance exists, which
.IR hoc (2)
has no reason to know about); the command text itself is entirely
.IR plot (2)'s
language, untouched here.
.PP
This file never touches a
.B "ref Hoc->Expr"
or
.BR Sym ,
never compiles anything, and never loads or names
.IR eqn2hoc (2)
\(em it only ever reads the plain data
.IR hoc (2)
hands back once a script has finished running (param labels/values/
bounds, observable labels, state count, max time) to build its Tk
sliders and drive its own integration loop.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/aerobraking.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR hoc (2),
.IR plot (2),
.IR tk (2),
.IR eqnorbitaltest (1)
.SH BUGS
The "planet" body's four state components never move \(em a real
property of this specific model, not a limitation of the command
language, which allows any number of
.B state
commands but has nothing yet exercising real N-body coupling through
it.
